<edge source="2D_GAF_d28aa344" target="2D_GAF_d28aa344" id="memorize_finding(finding=Cycle 6 on 2D_GAF NPY_nature_30_classes...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Cycle 6 on 2D_GAF NPY_nature_30_classes...)</data>
  <data key="d4">2</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], [-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Cycle 6 on 2D_GAF NPY_nature_30_classes: New best HO=0.4350 achieved with num_conv_layers=3, filters=64, lr=0.0003, dropout=0.7, batch_norm=1. This surpasses Cycle 5's 0.4257. However, CV=0.8980 means the CV-HO gap remains 0.4630 \u2014 overfitting is unchanged despite varying depth (3-4), filters (48-64), dropout (0.4-0.7), and lr (1e-4 to 3e-4). The gap never dropped below 0.44 in 9 trials this cycle. Stronger regularization (weight_decay, lower capacity) remains untested. O4 (weight_decay=0.1, dropout=0.7) and O3 (gaf_image_size=32, num_conv_layers=5) were not executed due to budget limits. The Optuna sweep (O2) failed with internal error '_missing_from_sweep' and was not retried. Root cause of data leakage still undiagnosed \u2014 all architecture tuning is likely futile until split contamination is fixed.", "category": "pipeline_results", "experiment_name": "2D_GAF", "_data_source": "NPY_nature_30_classes", "_manifest_name": "NPY_nature_30_classes", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 32, "video_num_segments": 1, "video_gaf_image_size": 128, "representation_type": "2D_GAF"}}</data>
