  <data key="d7">{"finding": "8 conv layers on hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py with 2D_GAF produced HO=0.3850, CV=0.8974 (gap=0.5124). This is WORSE than the 0.424 baseline gap \u2014 deeper layers amplified overfitting instead of reducing it. The architecture's attention mechanism may be memorizing training patterns rather than generalizing. Hypothesis: the model needs stronger regularization (dropout &gt;= 0.7, weight_decay &gt;= 0.05) or the 2D_GAF representation itself leaks train-set information into the held-out split.", "category": "overfitting_analysis", "experiment_name": "hybrid_d_gaf_attention_cnn.py", "_data_source": "NPY_nature_30_classes", "_manifest_name": "NPY_nature_30_classes", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 32, "video_num_segments": 1, "video_gaf_image_size": 128, "representation_type": "2D_GAF"}}</data>
